[{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6536812972", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6536812972", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6536812972, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhZ_ZrA", "user": {"login": "hafid-logic", "id": 266947999, "node_id": "U_kgDOD-lNnw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266947999?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic", "html_url": "https://github.com/hafid-logic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T00:55:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T00:55:19Z", "body": "Thanks @veighnsche for referencing this in #5; it fits under F0/F7.\n\nTo make it easy to verify, the difference is in hw/virtio/virtio.c, function virtio_add_queue:\n- v10.0.10, v10.0.12 and v10.1.0 use the requested queue_size;\n- v10.0.13 sets queue_size = VIRTQUEUE_MAX_SIZE (1024) unconditionally (code comment: \"Always set to max queue size for qemu <11.1\").\n\nSo only that stable point release trips the assertion. Caveat: I compared the QEMU sources, but I have not yet re-run Ginux's gates on 10.0.12 or 10.1.0.\n\nTwo minimal options, your call: (1) have verify_network_queue_rejections accept any power of two >= 8, like the init path already does; (2) print the QEMU version in make doctor and warn on known-incompatible versions.\n\nHappy to send a small PR for (1) if that fits your F0 plan. Just tell me the branch and style you prefer.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6536812972/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6540049160", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6540049160", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6540049160, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhdE7CA", "user": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T06:24:03Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T06:24:03Z", "body": "Thank you for the precise report. I confirmed that the runtime initialization path already accepts supported power-of-two queue sizes, while verify_network_queue_rejections alone required exactly 256 entries.\n\nPR #10 updates that verification to use the shared queue-size validator. It explicitly covers 1024 as valid and 1000 as invalid while retaining the existing zero, undersized, and non-power-of-two rejection checks:\nhttps://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/10\n\nValidation completed successfully with make architecture-check and make check. I am leaving this issue open while the PR is reviewed.", "author_association": "OWNER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6540049160/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6540517153", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6540517153", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6540517153, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhdhfIQ", "user": {"login": "hafid-logic", "id": 266947999, "node_id": "U_kgDOD-lNnw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266947999?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic", "html_url": "https://github.com/hafid-logic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T07:17:12Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T07:17:12Z", "body": "Thanks for the quick fix. PR #10 matches what I had in mind: the verification now uses the same validator as the init path, and the 1024/1000 cases make the contract explicit.\n\nOne note: make check passes even on QEMU 10.0.13 under TCG, so it does not exercise the runtime gates that were failing. I will try to run them on the PR branch under 10.0.13 (and 10.1.0 for comparison) and report here whether boot gets past this point, or what fails next.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6540517153/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6541969263", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6541969263", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6541969263, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhe6Hbw", "user": {"login": "hafid-logic", "id": 266947999, "node_id": "U_kgDOD-lNnw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266947999?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic", "html_url": "https://github.com/hafid-logic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T09:59:20Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T09:59:20Z", "body": "Thanks for PR #10. I validated it on QEMU 10.0.13 and 10.1.0 (official tarballs, TCG, 3 runs per cell) against its parent 22d20a63.\n\n- make run: the parent fails 3/3 on 10.0.13 with \"virtio network initialization invariant failed\"; the PR boots to the controller prompt 3/3. On 10.1.0 both boot 3/3.\n- make test still fails 3/3 on PR + 10.0.13, because tests/qemu/boot.sh:164-165 still grep for \"queue size: 256\" (the guest prints 1024). On 10.1.0, make test passes for both parent and PR.\n- On PR + 10.0.13, test-storage, test-rocky-shell, test-rocky-systemd and test-multi-domain pass.\n\nSo the kernel fix works, but the verification script needs the same relaxation. Happy to send a small patch for boot.sh if useful.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6541969263/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6545790806", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6545790806", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6545790806, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhijXVg", "user": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer", "html_url": "https://github.c