"starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gmkurtzer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T17:06:39Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T17:06:39Z", "body": "Gate 19 now implements the residual host-verifier fix in [PR #13](https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/13). Both receive and transmit checks accept the kernel-supported power-of-two range from 8 through 32768, including 1024, while rejecting invalid sizes and tolerating serial carriage returns. Exact pattern probes, `make check`, and the complete QEMU 10.1.2 `make test` passed (`GINUX_KERNEL_OK`; `Boot test passed.`). The PR is open for maintainer review; an exact QEMU 10.0.13 rerun remains useful but the contributor’s prior evidence directly covers that version. No merge or close action was taken.", "author_association": "OWNER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6546511460/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6546849960", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6546849960", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6546849960, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABhjkAqA", "user": {"login": "gmkurtzer", "id": 13984965, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTg0OTY1", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13984965?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://