owers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:55:22Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T20:55:22Z", "body": "Thanks, and no worries about the automation, it was fast!\n\nFor transparency: I had also prepared and verified a small boot.sh patch for this (same logic: accept any power of two >= 8 for the receive/transmit checks). With it applied on top of 759cf2e2, make test passed 3/3 on QEMU 10.0.13 (guest reports 1024) and 3/3 on 10.1.0 (256), TCG. I ran out of time before opening the PR, and #13 landed first, so please go with #13 and ignore mine.\n\nI read the #13 diff and it looks right to me: both checks accept 8 through 32768 and tolerate a trailing CR. I have not yet run #13 itself on 10.0.13.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6549015089/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6566218531", "html_url": "https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4#issuecomment-6566218531", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/4", "id": 6566218531, "node_id": "IC_kwDOVESuUM8AAAABh2CLIw", "user": {"login": "hafid-logic", "id": 266947999, "node_id": "U_kgDOD-lNnw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266947999?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic", "html_url": "https://github.com/hafid-logic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hafid-logic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-11-02T00:31:20Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-02T00:31:20Z", "body": "Thanks for the quick fixes, Gregory. PR #10 (kernel) and #13 (boot.sh) are merged, and make test passes on main@fbe6472e with QEMU 10.0.13 (queue size 1024) and 10.1.2 (256), TCG: https://github.com/hafid-logic/ginux-watch/actions/runs/41364863523. Closing this as resolved; happy to reopen if it regresses.", "author_association": "NONE", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gmkurtzer/ginux/issues/comments/6566218531/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]
